<section class="page-hero">
  <div id="ambient-canvas" class="ambient-canvas"></div>
  <div class="container page-hero-inner">
    <span class="eyebrow">Free Tool</span>
    <h1>Free Social Share Preview Generator</h1>
    <p>This <strong>free social share preview tool</strong> shows exactly how your link will look when shared on Facebook, LinkedIn, and X (Twitter) — plus the exact Open Graph tags to paste into your page. No signup, nothing leaves your browser.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="container contact-grid llms-tool-grid">
    <div>
      <form class="contact-form llms-form" id="og-form" onsubmit="return false;" aria-label="Social share preview form">
        <div>
          <label for="og-url">Page URL</label>
          <input type="text" id="og-url" placeholder="https://example.com/blog/post" value="https://contomatix.com/">
        </div>
        <div>
          <label for="og-title">Title</label>
          <input type="text" id="og-title" placeholder="Your page title" value="Contomatix — Link Building & SEO Services">
        </div>
        <div>
          <label for="og-desc">Description</label>
          <textarea id="og-desc" placeholder="A one to two sentence summary of the page.">Contomatix helps brands grow organic traffic through link building, guest posting, on-page and off-page SEO, and keyword research.</textarea>
        </div>
        <div>
          <label for="og-image">Image URL</label>
          <input type="text" id="og-image" placeholder="https://example.com/images/cover.jpg">
        </div>
        <div>
          <label>Preview platform</label>
          <div style="display:flex; gap:10px; flex-wrap: wrap;">
            <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary btn-sm" id="og-btn-facebook" data-platform="facebook">Facebook</button>
            <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline btn-sm" id="og-btn-linkedin" data-platform="linkedin">LinkedIn</button>
            <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline btn-sm" id="og-btn-twitter" data-platform="twitter">X / Twitter</button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </form>
    </div>

    <div class="contact-info-card llms-preview-card">
      <div class="llms-preview-head">
        <strong id="og-platform-label">Facebook preview</strong>
        <span id="og-status" class="llms-status">Live</span>
      </div>
      <div id="og-card" class="og-card">
        <div id="og-card-image" class="og-card-image">No image set</div>
        <div class="og-card-body">
          <div id="og-card-domain" class="og-card-domain">example.com</div>
          <div id="og-card-title" class="og-card-title">Your title will appear here</div>
          <div id="og-card-desc" class="og-card-desc">Your description will appear here.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="llms-hint" style="margin-top:14px;">Generated tags:</p>
      <pre id="og-output" class="llms-output" style="max-height:180px;"></pre>
      <div class="llms-actions">
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline btn-sm" id="og-copy">Copy Tags</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="container llms-explainer">

    <h2>What Are Open Graph Tags?</h2>
    <p>Open Graph tags are meta tags (originally created by Facebook, now used by nearly every platform) that control how your page appears when someone shares its link — the title, description, and image shown in the preview card. Without them, platforms fall back to guessing from your page's regular title tag and a random image, which often looks broken or unappealing.</p>

    <h2>Why the Preview Card Matters</h2>
    <p>A link with a missing or ugly preview gets fewer clicks than one with a clear title, compelling description, and a real image — this is true across social platforms, Slack, WhatsApp, and even some search engines that surface OG data. Since the card is often the only thing a scrolling user sees before deciding to click, it functions as free ad copy for every share your content gets.</p>

    <h2>Image Size Recommendations</h2>
    <ul class="service-points">
      <li><strong>Minimum: 1200 x 630px</strong> — the current standard recommended by Facebook and LinkedIn for a crisp, non-cropped card</li>
      <li><strong>Aspect ratio: 1.91:1</strong> — images with a different ratio get cropped unpredictably by different platforms</li>
      <li><strong>Keep text off the edges</strong> — some platforms crop image corners on certain devices; keep any text or logos centered</li>
      <li><strong>Use an absolute URL</strong> — a relative image path (like "/images/cover.jpg") will not resolve correctly when a crawler outside your domain reads it</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Free Social Share Preview FAQs</h2>
    <div class="faq-list" style="margin-top: 22px;">
      <details>
        <summary>Why does my link still show an old preview after I updated the tags?<span class="faq-icon"></span></summary>
        <p>Most platforms cache the preview the first time a link is shared and won't re-check it automatically. Use each platform's own debugging tool (Facebook Sharing Debugger, LinkedIn Post Inspector) to force a re-scrape after changes.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Do I need separate tags for Twitter/X?<span class="faq-icon"></span></summary>
        <p>X reads its own <code>twitter:card</code> meta tags but falls back to standard Open Graph tags if those aren't present. Adding both gives you more control over how the X-specific card renders.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Does this affect my SEO or search rankings?<span class="faq-icon"></span></summary>
        <p>Not directly — Open Graph tags aren't a ranking factor. They do affect click-through rate on social shares, which can indirectly support traffic and engagement signals.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What happens if I don't set an og:image?<span class="faq-icon"></span></summary>
        <p>Most platforms will either show no image at all, or attempt to auto-select an image from the page — often with unpredictable and unflattering results. Always set one explicitly.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Does this tool store or send my data anywhere?<span class="faq-icon"></span></summary>
        <p>No. Everything is generated in your browser with JavaScript — nothing is uploaded, logged, or stored on any server, including ours.</p>
      </details>
    </div>

    <div class="cta-band" style="margin-top: 44px;">
      <span class="cta-orb cta-orb-1"></span>
      <span class="cta-orb cta-orb-2"></span>
      <h2>Want every share of your content to convert?</h2>
      <p>Contomatix optimizes on-page and social metadata across your whole site.</p>
      <div class="cta-actions">
        <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Get in touch</a>
        <a href="https://wa.me/<%= site.whatsappNumber %>" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-glass">Chat on WhatsApp</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

